"To find \\( f(-10) \\), we need to determine which piece of the piecewise function to use. The function \\( f(x) \\) is defined as follows:\n\n\\[\nf(x) =\n\\begin{cases}\n3x + 5 & \\text{if } x < -3, \\\\\n7 - 4x & \\text{if } x \\ge -3.\n\\end{cases}\n\\]\n\nSince \\( -10 \\) is less than \\( -3 \\), we use the first piece of the function:\n\n\\[\nf(-10) = 3(-10) + 5\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform the multiplication:\n\n\\[\n3(-10) = -30\n\\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[\nf(-10) = -30 + 5\n\\]\n\nNext, we perform the addition:\n\n\\[\n-30 + 5 = -25\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( f(-10) \\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{-25\n\\]\\]\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $-25\\). I hope it is correct."
"To evaluate the expression \\(a^3 \\cdot a^2\\) when \\(a = 5\\), we can follow these steps:\n\n1. Simplify the expression \\(a^3 \\cdot a^2\\) using the properties of exponents.\n2. Substitute \\(a = 5\\) into the simplified expression.\n\nFirst, let's simplify \\(a^3 \\cdot a^2\\):\n\nThe property of exponents that states \\(a^m \\cdot a^n = a^{m+n}\\) allows us to combine the exponents:\n\n\\[\na^3 \\cdot a^2 = a^{3+2} = a^5\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute \\(a = 5\\) into the expression \\(a^5\\):\n\n\\[\na^5 = 5^5\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate \\(5^5\\):\n\n\\[\n5^5 = 5 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 5 = 3125\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final value of \\(a^3 \\cdot a^2\\) when \\(a = 5\\) is \\(\\boxed{3125}\\)."
