"To solve the expression \\((34-10)+(20-9)+(55-10)\\) in your head, we can break it down into smaller steps and compute each part individually.\n\n1. Compute \\(34 - 10\\):\n   \\[\n   34 - 10 = 24\n   \\]\n\n2. Compute \\(20 - 9\\):\n   \\[\n   20 - 9 = 11\n   \\]\n\n3. Compute \\(55 - 10\\):\n   \\[\n   55 - 10 = 45\n   \\]\n\nNow, we add these results together:\n\\[\n24 + 11 + 45\n\\]\n\nFirst, add \\(24\\) and \\(11\\):\n\\[\n24 + 11 = 35\n\\]\n\nNext, add the result of \\(24 + 11\\) to \\(45\\):\n\\[\n35 + 45 = 80\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{80}\n\\]"
