"We need to find the values of \\( k \\) for which the arithmetic sequence \\( S_k \\) contains the term 2005. The sequence \\( S_k \\) is defined as:\n\n\\[ S_k = 1 + (n-1) \\cdot k \\]\n\nWe need to find \\( n \\) such that \\( S_k = 2005 \\):\n\n\\[ 1 + (n-1) \\cdot k = 2005 \\]\n\nRearranging the equation:\n\n\\[ (n-1) \\cdot k = 2004 \\]\n\nSince \\( n-1 \\) must be an integer, \\( k \\) must be a divisor of 2004. We need to find all positive divisors of 2004.\n\nThe prime factorization of 2004 is:\n\n\\[ 2004 = 2^3 \\times 251 \\]\n\nThe divisors of 2004 are 1, 2, 4, 251, and 2004.\n\nThus, the number of values of \\( k \\) is \\(\\boxed{4}\\)."
