"To compute \\(\\tan 45^\\circ\\), we can use the definition of the tangent function, which is the ratio of the sine of the angle to the cosine of the angle.\n\nFor \\(45^\\circ\\), we know that:\n\\[\n\\sin 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the tangent of \\(45^\\circ\\) is:\n\\[\n\\tan 45^\\circ = \\frac{\\sin 45^\\circ}{\\cos 45^\\circ} = \\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}}{\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}} = 1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(\\tan 45^\\circ\\) is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $1$. I hope it is correct."
