"The reflection matrix over a vector $\\begin{pmatrix} a \\\\ b \\end{pmatrix}$ is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{R} = \\frac{1}{1 - a^2 - b^2} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -b \\\\ -b & a \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFor the vector $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ 5 \\end{pmatrix}$, we have $a = 1$ and $b = 5$. Substituting these values into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{R} = \\frac{1}{1 - 1^2 - 5^2} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{1}{-24} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe determinant of this matrix is:\n\n\\[\n\\det \\mathbf{R} = \\frac{1}{-24} \\cdot (1)(1) - (-5)(-5) = \\frac{-24}{-2} = 1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{1}$."
"To find the equation of the parabola, we need to eliminate the parameter \\( t \\) from the given parametric equations. The parametric equations are:\n\n\\[ x = 2t + 5 \\]\n\\[ y = 12t^2 - 8t - 7 \\]\n\nFirst, solve for \\( t \\) in terms of \\( x \\):\n\n\\[ t = \\frac{x - 5}{2} \\]\n\nNext, substitute this expression for \\( t \\) into the equation for \\( y \\):\n\n\\[ y = 12\\left(\\frac{x - 5}{2}\\right)^2 - 8\\left(\\frac{x - 5}{2}\\right) - 7 \\]\n\nSimplify the equation:\n\n\\[ y = 3(x - 5)^2 - 4(x - 5) - 7 \\]\n\\[ y = 3x^2 - 30x + 75 - 4x + 20 - 7 \\]\n\\[ y = 3x^2 - 34x + 88 \\]\n\nThis is the equation of the parabola. I hope this solution is correct."
