"To find the dot product of the vectors \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 7 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we multiply the corresponding components and then sum the results.\n\nThe dot product of two vectors \\(\\begin{pmatrix} a_1 \\\\ b_2 \\\\ a_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\begin{pmatrix} b_1 \\\\ b_2 \\\\ b_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is given by:\n\\[\na_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + a_3 b_3\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given vectors:\n\\[\n(-2)(3) + (0)(4) + (7)(-5)\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n\\[\n(-2)(3) = -6\n\\]\n\\[\n(0)(4) = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n(7)(-5) = -35\n\\]\n\nAdding these results together:\n\\[\n-6 + 0 - 35 = -41\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the dot product of the vectors is \\(\\boxed{-41}\\)."
"We have that $\\text{proj}_{\\bold{w}} \\bold{v} = \\frac{\\bold{v} \\cdot \\bold{w}}{\\bold{w} \\cdot \\bold{w}} \\bold{w}$.\n\nFirst, we compute $\\bold{v} \\cdot \\bold{w}$ and $\\bold{w} \\cdot \\bold{w}$:\n\n$\\bold{v} \\cdot \\bold{w} = (2)(2) + (3)(-1) + (-1)(0) = 4 - 3 + 0 = 1$\n\n$\\bold{w} \\cdot \\bold{w} = (2)(2) + (-1)(-1) + (0)(0) = 4 + 1 + 0 = 5$\n\nNow, we substitute these values into the formula:\n\n$\\text{proj}_{\\bold{w}} \\bold{v} = \\frac{1}{5} \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}$\n\nTherefore, the final answer is $\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ 0 \\end{pmatrix}}$."
